  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "The current best (config_045: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted; acc=0.713) shows that multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the dominant driver of performance. However, in singleprofile, RNA alone (0.520) was nearly as strong as multimodal (0.532–0.540), while image-only was very weak (0.227), suggesting the image modality contributes little. The critical open question is whether this pattern holds in the multiprofile+transformer regime, where cross-modal interaction dynamics may differ. config_024 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean one-variable ablation of the image modality from the current best. If it approaches ~0.70, the image modality is redundant and future effort should focus on RNA encoder and aggregation refinements; if it drops substantially, the image modality becomes essential in multiprofile and we should optimize the image encoder. This single experiment resolves a fundamental design decision (is multimodality needed?) that will shape all remaining budget allocation, making it the highest-information experiment available."
}

